# Inspector Panel Ownership (`MOD-12`)

Follow `/docs/standards/12-inspector-panel-ownership-and-ui-shell.md`.

## Tab ownership

| Tab | Owns | Never hosts |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Overview | Roadmap Story + Technical (Formula A2), topology directory, Steps titles/MITRE only | Stage Filter, Cascading Process, VAD, Memory callouts, stage-titled headers, deep-dives, duplicate title card |
| Steps | Per-stage deep-dives + Visual State Machine + merged stage pills | Full PPID→PID cascade, Auto-Play, legend cards, standalone Stage Filter |
| Process Hierarchy | Cascade tree + merged title/stage pills (embedded rows) | VAD mutation, nested MiniMap title card, stacked process sub-cards |
| Memory | VAD + memoryBlocks | Cascading Process waterfall |
| SIEM Logs / Sources | Logs / intel only | Attack mechanics dumps |

## Single-card merge law

- Overview (main): badge + title + Story/Technical = **one** card.
- Steps: `inspector-steps-merged-shell` with header pills; hide global Stage Filter.
- Process Hierarchy: one shell; `cascadingProcessEmbedded: true`; hide global Stage Filter.
- Standalone Stage Filter only on Memory / SIEM Logs / Sources.

## Chrome laws

- Sidebar labels: bare names — never `Memory (3)`.
- Steps: no Auto-Play; no legend trio.
- Migrate before delete (`MOD-11` §7). Cascade → Process Hierarchy.

## Code layout

`components/inspector/**`; public entry `components/InspectorPanel.tsx` re-exports. Tests use `readInspectorSources()`.
